§ `CODEX Insurance Limited - Hospitalization Policy`

§§ `Claim record - the facts needed to decide whether a claim is covered`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `age at hospitalization`                            IS A NUMBER
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`    IS A NUMBER
    sickness                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `accidental injury`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from skydiving`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service in the military`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service in the police`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud misrepresentation or withholding`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `wellness visit months after effective date`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `wellness confirmation months after effective date` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

§§ `1.3 - wellness visit no later than the 6th month anniversary, confirmed no later than the 7th`

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit was on time` c IS
    CONSIDER (c's `wellness visit months after effective date`)
    WHEN JUST v THEN v AT MOST 6
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit was late` c IS
    CONSIDER (c's `wellness visit months after effective date`)
    WHEN JUST v THEN v GREATER THAN 6
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness confirmation was on time` c IS
    CONSIDER (c's `wellness confirmation months after effective date`)
    WHEN JUST k THEN k AT MOST 7
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness confirmation was late` c IS
    CONSIDER (c's `wellness confirmation months after effective date`)
    WHEN JUST k THEN k GREATER THAN 7
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 satisfied in a timely fashion` c IS
    `wellness visit was on time` c
    AND `wellness confirmation was on time` c

-- Once either the visit or its confirmation is definitely known to have
-- happened too late, no later event can cure it: the condition can never be
-- satisfied in a timely fashion, no matter what else happens.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 has not been satisfied in a timely fashion` c IS
    `wellness visit was late` c
    OR `wellness confirmation was late` c

§§ `1.1(3) - the condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending, or has been satisfied`

-- "Still pending" at the time of the hospitalization means: nothing yet
-- known makes satisfaction impossible, AND the final (7th month) deadline
-- has not yet passed as of that hospitalization. Note this compares the
-- hospitalization time only against the fixed 7-month threshold from the
-- text, never against another claimant-supplied relative time.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 is still pending` c IS
    NOT `condition 1-3 satisfied in a timely fashion` c
    AND NOT `condition 1-3 has not been satisfied in a timely fashion` c
    AND c's `months after effective date of hospitalization` AT MOST 7

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 is pending or has been satisfied` c IS
    `condition 1-3 satisfied in a timely fashion` c
    OR `condition 1-3 is still pending` c

§§ `1.2 / 3.6 - cancelation and the one-year policy term`

-- Section 3.6: the term is one year (12 months) from the effective date.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy term has expired` c IS
    c's `months after effective date of hospitalization` GREATER THAN 12

-- Section 1.2: cancelation is deemed to occur on fraud, misrepresentation or
-- material withholding of information, on failure to satisfy Section 1.3 in
-- a timely fashion, or automatically at the end of the policy term.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy has been canceled` c IS
    c's `fraud misrepresentation or withholding`
    OR `condition 1-3 has not been satisfied in a timely fashion` c
    OR `policy term has expired` c

§§ `1.1 - policy in effect at the time of the hospitalization`

-- Section 1.1 conditions (1) the agreement is signed and (2) the premium has
-- been paid are, per the task instructions, assumed always TRUE and are not
-- encoded here.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy is in effect at the hospitalization` c IS
    `condition 1-3 is pending or has been satisfied` c
    AND NOT `policy has been canceled` c

§§ `2.1 - general exclusions`

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `age exclusion applies` c IS
    c's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- Items (1)-(4) of Section 2.1 all share the "arising directly or
-- indirectly out of" causal chapeau: the hospitalization must actually
-- arise from the named activity, not merely coincide with the claimant's
-- occupation or pastime at the time.
GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `event is excluded` c IS
    c's `arose from skydiving`
    OR c's `arose from service in the military`
    OR c's `arose from service as a fire fighter`
    OR c's `arose from service in the police`
    OR `age exclusion applies` c

§§ `3.1 - territorial scope`
-- "Your Policy insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the
-- world." Coverage is worldwide and unconditional, so no exclusion or
-- Claim field is needed to represent location.

§§ `1.1 - the hospitalization must be for sickness or accidental injury`

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` c IS
    c's sickness
    OR c's `accidental injury`

§§ `Top-level decision`

GIVEN c IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` c IS
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` c
    AND `policy is in effect at the hospitalization` c
    AND NOT `event is excluded` c
